xteetotaller is a Wine prefix manager.
Current version is 0.1.
This software is still in Alpha state, use at your own risk.

The only required dependencies are Motif and standard X11 libraries.
It requires a C99-compliant compiler with some parts of the Single Unix
Specification, Version 3 (also known as POSIX.1-2001), implemented.

xteetotaller is meant to be used on an x86 CPU.
Using this program on any other CPU architecture may cause issues.

Third-party libraries licenses are present in the licenses subdirectory.
Building and installation information are available in the INSTALL file.

Winetricks must be installed on the system where xteetotaller is used.

Features
========
* Lightweight GUI created with Motif
* Low number of dependencies - only Motif and X11 libraries
* win32, win64 and wow64 Wine prefixes creation
* Programs list for each prefix
* Enabling and disabling DXVK dlls
* Switching prefix Wine version
* Setting launch options for each program
* Enabling the experimental WineD3D Damavand renderer for specific programs
* Setting X11 DISPLAY per program
* Disabling winemenubuilder for each prefix
* No internet access, no automatic downloads

Planned features
================
* Set dll overrides for each program
* Set environment variables for prefixes
* Set niceness value for each program
* In-program help system

Known issues
============
* It is not possible to copy and paste with Ctrl+C and Ctrl+V yet.
However, it is possible to copy and paste with middle click like all X11
programs do.
IBM Common User Access keyboard shortcuts for Cut/Copy/Paste such as Shift+Ins
are also supported.
* Some parts of the program could have their number of memory allocations
reduced.
A lot of allocations are made in a naive way, where blocks are resized by one
when an object is added.
This is unnoticeable for the user in most cases, but must still be addressed.
* There are no documentation or help system for the program.
* Labels with UTF-8 characters may not be displayed correctly.
However, this isssue should not be present on TextField widgets.
* Some fonts are hardcoded and cannot be modified with Xt resources.
* Some errors may result in crash or are ignored silently.
The former is mostly caused by a configuration file writing error.
This should not happen unless the file system is corrupted or has not enough
free space, or the files have incorrect permissions.
This is not a big issue as the user will probably notice these issues on
other programs before launching xteetotaller or will be the result of their own actions.
* There are TOCTOU vulnerabilities.
Wine and DXVK versions and prefix and programs information are read during the
launch of xteetotaller.
These should not be deleted or modified by an external tool while xteetotaller
is running.
However, it is safe to delete Wine, DXVK, program configuration files and
prefixes directories when xteetotaller is closed.
* Pure 64-bit Wine versions are not supported. This means that Wine builds
that cannot run 32-bit executables will not be detected correctly by this
program. In practice, a pure 64-bit build is useless as many 64-bit programs
require 32-bit components. Use Wow64 builds instead.

